  "notes": [
    "[THIS PRODUCT] Harvested from mountain forest wildflowers, this raw honey contains a single ingredient with no added syrups, artificial flavorings, or preservatives.",
    "[GENERAL] Unlike conventional processed honey, raw honey is unpasteurized and minimally filtered, preserving delicate floral aromatics that high-heat processing flattens or strips away.",
    "[GENERAL] When sweetening hot tea, coffee, or matcha, let the drink cool slightly below boiling (ideally below 110°F–140°F / 43°C–60°C) before stirring in raw honey to keep high heat from muting its nuanced aromatics.",
    "[GENERAL] Natural crystallization over time into a thick or semi-solid state is a normal physical property of raw honey and is not a sign of spoilage.",
    "[GENERAL] To reliquefy crystallized raw honey without degrading its flavor profile, place the sealed jar in a warm water bath heated between 95°F and 110°F (35°C–43°C) until smooth.",
    "[GENERAL] Raw honey should be kept at room temperature in a cool, dry pantry rather than refrigerated, as temperatures below 60°F (15°C) accelerate crystallization."
